TERMS AND CONDITIONS

1. PERMITTED USE

You are free to:

a) Use, copy, modify, merge, publish, and distribute the Software for your own internal
   business purposes or personal, non-commercial purposes. This includes:
   - An individual using Flowcomments for their personal Instagram accounts
   - A company deploying Flowcomments to automate its own Instagram business accounts
   - An agency or freelancer running Flowcomments on their own infrastructure to manage
     their own Instagram accounts or their clients' Instagram accounts as part of their
     general service offering, provided they do not charge separately for access to the
     Software itself

b) Study how the Software works and adapt it to your needs

c) Self-host the Software on your own infrastructure or any infrastructure you control

2. RESTRICTIONS

You may NOT, without obtaining a separate commercial license from the Licensor:

a) Sell, rent, lease, sublicense, or otherwise offer the Software (in original or modified
   form) to third parties as a standalone paid product, hosted service, or SaaS offering

b) Make the Software available as a service or hosted offering where the primary value
   proposition to users is access to the Software itself, whether free or paid

c) White-label or rebrand the Software for distribution or service provision to others

d) Charge third parties specifically for access to, or use of, the Software (though you may
   charge for other services that happen to use the Software as an internal tool)

e) Use the Software as part of a product or service that competes with Flowcomments or
   any official offerings from the Licensor

f) Copy, fork, or redistribute the Software (original or modified) primarily to resell,
   rebrand, or commercially exploit it as a substitute for Flowcomments Cloud or the
   official self-host edition, including private “clone and charge” deployments offered
   to third parties as access to the Software

g) Strip, obfuscate, or systematically disable the required attribution notices, copyright
   headers, or the anonymous installation identity / telemetry mechanisms included to
   support license compliance and community metrics, except where the Licensor has granted
   a separate commercial license

3. ATTRIBUTION AND BRANDING REQUIREMENTS

a) You must retain all copyright notices, license notices, and attribution present in the
   Software

b) You must keep the "Flowcomments" name, logo, and "Powered by Flowcomments" notice
   visible and unmodified in the Software's user interface, including but not limited to:
   - The footer of all pages
   - The settings/about section
   - The console output (where applicable)

c) These attribution elements must remain clearly visible to end users and administrators

d) Removing, modifying, obscuring, or making these elements non-visible requires a separate
   commercial license from the Licensor

e) Official builds may report an anonymous installation identifier, software version, and
   coarse operational metrics (for example public hostname and connected account counts) to
   the Licensor’s control plane for install metrics and license compliance. This does not
   include your Instagram content, message bodies, or end-user personal data. You may disable
   telemetry with FLOWCOMMENTS_TELEMETRY=false; doing so does not waive Sections 2–3.

